    "title": "Kardashian Jewelry Robbery Trial Details",
    "text": "• Reality television star Kim Kardashian was robbed of jewelry worth millions of dollars in Paris.\n• Kardashian's attorney, Michael Rhodes, announced she will testify on May 13 during a trial scheduled from April 28 to May 23 in Paris.\n• Rhodes stated that Kardashian has 'tremendous appreciation and admiration for the French judicial system.'\n• The robbery occurred in Kardashian's Paris apartment during Paris Fashion Week.\n• Several masked men, some impersonating police officers, entered her residence, gagged her, tied her up, and locked her in a bathroom.\n• The thieves stole several pieces of jewelry, including a $4 million ring given to her by ex-husband Kanye West.\n• Seventeen individuals were arrested in connection with the theft in January 2017.\n• Four suspects were indicted in January 2017, with 10 individuals now facing charges of armed robbery, kidnapping, and membership in a criminal gang.\n• Aomar Ait Khedache, known as 'Old Omar,' is alleged to be the ringleader of the gang.\n• Some thieves lost stolen items while fleeing, including suspect Yunice Abbas, who dropped a diamond-encrusted cross worth over $30,000.\n• It is unclear if Khedache and Abbas are among the 10 individuals being tried, or if others involved will be tried later.",
